 "_id": "KdemmuLMMISHWRIP",
 "name": "Madness Inducement",
 "type": "spell",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/faceless-god.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Faceless God — Innate Technique (1st level)</em></p><blockquote><p>Just a glance in your direction slowly leads to mental corruption.</p></blockquote><p>Starting at 1st level, just looking at you slowly leads to mental corruption. As an action for 3 cursed energy, you can activate your technique for 1 minute causing madness to spread to everyone around you. If a creature ends their turn within 60 ft of you and can see you, it gains a 5% increase to Mental Corruption. You can choose a number of creatures to be immune to this effect when you activate the technique.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Corruption Rate</th>\n<th>Effect</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">10%</td>\n<td>-1 to AC</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">20%</td>\n<td>-1 to saves</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">25%</td>\n<td>Roll D10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">30%</td>\n<td>-4 to passive Perception</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">40%</td>\n<td>-2 to AC and saves</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">50%</td>\n<td>Roll D6, Can’t maintain Concentration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">60%</td>\n<td>Disadvantage on skill checks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">70%</td>\n<td>Charmed by you</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">75%</td>\n<td>Roll D4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">80%</td>\n<td>-4 to AC and saves</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">90%</td>\n<td>Random Direction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">100%</td>\n<td>Can’t talk, only scream</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Paranoia and Madness</strong>. When a creature reaches 25% <em>Mental Corruption</em>, they begin seeing all creatures as faceless monsters and must roll a d10 at the start of their turn. On a roll of 1-2, the target spends their action attacking the closest creature. A creature can only have up to 25% <em>Mental Corruption</em> at a time.</p>\n<p><strong>Madness Removal</strong>. <em>Mental Corruption</em> persists even after your technique has been deactivated. A creature without line of sight to you can make a Wisdom saving throw to reduce <em>Mental Corruption</em> by 5% and repeat the save at the beginning of their turn. If a creature has more than 25% corruption, they cannot reduce corruption below 25% as the madness becomes rooted more deeply within their mind. As part of a long rest, they can attempt to make a Wisdom saving throw to cleanse their mind. On a success, they can begin making saves to reduce madness as normal, down to the next 25% segment before they must complete another long rest to repeat the save and continue to process.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
